      <div type="clause" n="20.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 20.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 20.3" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="560" ed="#liebermann"/>Singulorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.l"/> denique<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.28"/> baronum, senatorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.29"/> — clericorum, laicorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.30"/> —, ubicunque habeant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.31"/> terram, siue<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.32"/> socna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.33"/> regis sit uel non, in capitalibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="m" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.m"/> questionibus socna [regis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.34"/>] est, sicut a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.35"/> (Edmundi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.36"/>), Cnuti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.37"/> uel Edwardi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="n" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.n"/> legibus per successiones posteras hereditaria dignitas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.38"/> successit, nisi uel propinquitate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.39"/> uel aliqua dignitate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.40"/> meritorum regis indulgencia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.41"/> quemcumque respexerit, cuius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.42"/> amanda bonitas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="o" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.o"/> promouet potius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.43"/>, non euertit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.44"/> libertatem.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 560 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.l" n="l" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Optimaten, Kleriker oder Laien, stehen in Criminalsachen unter Königsgericht, auch wenn ihr Manor sonst unter privater Jurisdiction steht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Magnates, clerical or lay, are subject to the king's court in criminal matters, even if their manor is otherwise under private jurisdiction</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.m" n="m" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">deren Strafe Leben, Glieder oder Wergeld kostet oder</hi> in misericordia regis <hi rend="italic">verfällt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">whose punishment costs life, limbs or wergild, or falls in misericordia regis</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.n" n="n" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seit der Verfassung des Bekenners, <hi rend="italic">die Verf. auch sonst mit der Cnuts gleich setzt; vgl.</hi> Quadr. Arg. 1. 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">since the constitution of the Confessor, which the author elsewhere too equates with Cnut's; cf. Quadr. Arg. 1. 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.o" n="o" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Quadr. II Praef. 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Quadr. II Praef. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sc Hg add et</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">layc. <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">layc. Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">te. h. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">te. h. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sine <hi rend="italic">Wh</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sine Wh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sokna <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sokna Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hss.; ergänzt Wi Tho.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MSS; supplied by Wi Tho.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Sc Hg</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vielleicht vom Verfasser selbst nur nachgetragen; vgl.</hi> 88, 12]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Sc Hg [perhaps only added later by the author himself; cf. 88, 12]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Kn. <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> uel <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> comiti <hi rend="italic">Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Kn. without uel Lond; comiti Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.38" n="38" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tate <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tate Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-quante <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-quante Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">m. d. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">m. d. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">intelligentia quec. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">intelligentia quec. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.42" n="42" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cui <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cui Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt ein Corr. Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et inserted by a corrector Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.44" n="44" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tet <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tet Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">für <hi rend="italic">witan</hi> im Sinne der leitenden, angesehensten Gerichtsoberen <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 29, 4 und in Urkk. 9. 10. Jhs., auch Earle <hi rend="italic">Landchar</hi>. 70. 283, hier aber wohl auch ‘Reichsratsmitglieder’; <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. mein <hi rend="italic">National assembly</hi> p. 9{6}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for <hi rend="italic">witan</hi> in the sense of the leading, most respected presiding officers of the courts <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 29, 4 and in charters of the 9th and 10th cent., also Earle <hi rend="italic">Landchar</hi>. 70. 283; but here probably also ‘members of the king's council’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> my <hi rend="italic">National assembly</hi> p. 9{6}</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dass <hi rend="spaced">alle</hi> Kapitalverbrechen (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4b) dem Könige gehören, wie Frühere (auch Stubbs <hi rend="italic">Lect</hi>. 158) diese Stelle verstanden, steht zwar des Verf. Meinung nach einigen anderen Stellen ganz nahe. Hier aber will er so Allgemeines nicht sagen—der Zwischensatz <hi rend="italic">sive s. r. s. u. non</hi> wäre sonst sinnlos—, sondern laut des Zitats nur wegen des höchsten Status des Täters die Zuständigkeit dem Königsgericht (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8b) vorbehalten; <hi rend="italic">s. u</hi>. 24, 1 [Stubbs meinte jener Deutung zu Liebe, diese <hi rend="italic">senatores</hi> als niedere <hi rend="italic">þegnas</hi> von den höheren Magnaten in 20, 2 trennen zu sollen; allein <hi rend="italic">barones</hi> ohne Weiteres heisst bei Hn höchste Kronvassallen]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That <hi rend="italic">all</hi> capital crimes (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4b) belong to the king, as earlier scholars (Stubbs <hi rend="italic">Lect</hi>. 158 among them) understood this passage, is indeed very close to the author's view as expressed in some other passages. Here, however, he does not mean to say anything so general—the intervening clause <hi rend="italic">sive s. r. s. u. non</hi> would otherwise be meaningless—but, according to the citation, only to reserve jurisdiction to the king's court (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8b) on account of the offender's highest rank; <hi rend="italic">see below</hi> 24, 1 [For the sake of that interpretation Stubbs thought he had to separate these <hi rend="italic">senatores</hi>, as lesser <hi rend="italic">þegnas</hi>, from the higher magnates in 20, 2; but in Hn <hi rend="italic">barones</hi> without qualification means the highest tenants-in-chief of the Crown]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-3.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nur durch II Cn 13, 1 über Heimfall des Bocland an den König lag der Gedanke an den Adel des Täters nahe. Von Eadmund I., dessen Name der frühereren Rezension samt Rs fehlt, ist nichts hierauf Bezügliches uns bekannt. Ward der Name nur willkürlich nachgetragen? <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eadwardi laga 4c—<hi rend="italic">te. ha</hi>.{31}—<hi rend="italic">socna est</hi> ohne <hi rend="italic">regis</hi>{34}—<hi rend="italic">Eadw</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">dignitate</hi>{38} ‘wie es durch Thronfolge vererbte’—<hi rend="italic">m. d</hi>.{40} <hi rend="italic">r. i. quecumque</hi> Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Only II Cn 13, 1, on the forfeiture of bookland to the king, suggested the idea of the offender's noble rank. Of Eadmund I, whose name is lacking in the earlier recension together with Rs, nothing relevant to this is known to us. Was the name merely added arbitrarily? <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eadwardi laga 4c—<hi rend="italic">te. ha</hi>.{31}—<hi rend="italic">socna est</hi> without <hi rend="italic">regis</hi>{34}—<hi rend="italic">Eadw</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">dignitate</hi>{38} ‘as it was inherited through succession to the throne’—<hi rend="italic">m. d</hi>.{40} <hi rend="italic">r. i. quecumque</hi> Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
